    "desired": {
      "strategyPreset": "CUSTOM",
      "modelId": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6",
      "behavior": {
        "risk": "AGGRESSIVE",
        "outlook": "REALIST",
        "conviction": "MODERATE"
      },
      "contextSources": {
        "includeSubTimeframe": true,
        "includeRsi": true,
        "includeMacd": true,
        "includeVolume": true,
        "includeVolatility": true,
        "includeBollingerBands": true,
        "includeMovingAverages": true,
        "includeStochastic": false,
        "includeFundingRates": true,
        "includeOpenInterest": true,
        "includeRelativeStrength": true,
        "includeSupportResistance": true,
        "includeTrendStrength": true,
        "includeMfi": false,
        "includeHigherTimeframe": true,
        "includeRegimeContext": true,
        "includeStructureZones": true,
        "includeCrowdIntelligence": true,
        "includeCvd": true,
        "includeCvdCrowdConvergence": false,
        "includeMtfConfluence": true
      },
      "overlayText": "VOLATILIS \u2014 hourly volatility-capture.\n\nScoring: each correct call earns the coin's absolute % move over the 1h window; a wrong call loses the same; the Captain doubles both. Points come from MAGNITUDE, so hunt the biggest expected 1h movers and get their direction right.\n\nSELECTION \u2014 draft the 9 highest expected-points coins. Rank the pool by expected 1h move size: expanding volatility/ATR, Bollinger band-width squeeze-release, volume surges, open-interest build, and strong relative strength / rate-of-change vs peers \u2014 favoring coins already moving and accelerating on the recent 1h candles and sub-timeframe drift. Skip quiet, low-volatility coins even when direction seems obvious; a correct call on a flat coin barely scores.\n\nDIRECTION \u2014 evidence-based, no house bias. Read momentum (recent 1h candles, MACD, moving-average alignment) and CVD pressure; weigh higher-timeframe trend, trend strength/ADX, regime and multi-timeframe confluence. In trending/expansion regimes follow momentum and clean breakouts through structure zones; in ranging/contracting regimes respect mean-reversion at Bollinger and support/resistance extremes and demand more confluence. Fade over-extended, crowded moves into a level; back clean breakouts on rising participation and funding.\n\nCAPTAIN \u2014 the 2x lever, both ways. Captain the coin with the highest expected points = expected |move| x confidence: it must be BOTH a likely large mover AND high conviction, since a wrong volatile captain is doubled. Never captain a coin-flip. A correct top-moving captain also opens the Jackpot.\n\nCONFIDENCE \u2014 report your true calibrated 0-1 value: higher when volatility, momentum, trend, regime and structure agree; lower when they conflict or the tape is quiet. Never inflate to force a grid; never zero a genuine read."
    },
    "signalRules": [],
    "tradingConfig": {
      "manage": false
    }
  },
